! mcp_bootstrap_p177.strap -- THE IDENTIFIER, K FRONT, the head of the
! service-op identifier routine, printed page 177.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.177+7 = 184.  The header was READ at
! 600 dpi, not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LA000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  177".
!
! >>> A NEW CARD DECK BEGINS ON THIS PAGE: PREFIX "LA", SERIAL
! 000001. <<<  printed p.176 ended on KE0000106 -- read off that
! deck's own listing block, whose serials pair two lines to a card, so
! its lines 47-48 are KE0000106 and there is no 107.  The prefix changes
! AND the serial restarts at 1 on the very line that opens the
! asterisk banner, which is independent evidence that the IDENTIFIER
! is a section boundary and not a continuation of the F WIT tables.
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK. <<<
! Rendered at 600 dpi across the right-hand end of the form (crop
! x=7300 y=490 W=2900 H=140): the word "LOCATION" is printed and NO
! DIGITS FOLLOW IT, only the dashed rule.  Nothing was read off the
! rule and nothing was taken from any OCR.  That is exactly what
! docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1 predicts -- the field is LINE
! 1'S location, and line 1 here is an asterisk banner that compiles
! nothing.  A blank is NOT a zero.
!
! printed p.176's deck predicted this field would be blank, by that
! same rule, before this page was opened.  It is.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES ON FIFTY-FIVE CARDS, and then blank paper
! to the foot of the form.  Three asterisk-banner comment cards, one
! "SLC,$", and FIFTY-TWO instructions -- THIRTY-SIX half words and
! SIXTEEN full words.  That reconciles twice: 36 + 16 = 52 statements,
! and 36 + 2*16 = 68 half-word slots = 34 words.  The sixteen full
! words are the !CHECK rows below that carry FOUR printed tokens.  No DD, no SYN, no VF, no reservation, no
! forward SLC.  The page is CONTIGUOUS from 220700.00 through the
! end of word 220741, with no hole of any kind:
!
!     >>> 34 WORDS, 220700.00 .. 220741.00, COUNTER LEAVES AT
!         220742.00. <<<
!
! NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END.  Counted off the CARD-SERIAL column,
! not off the survey: LA000001 is on line 1 and LA000055 is on line
! 56, with the form's top and bottom rules both visible in the same
! render.  The serials run 1..55 with ONE repeat -- LA000048 prints
! TWICE, on lines 48 and 49 -- which is the semicolon one-card form
! printed p.176 established (its "SIC,STIC; BD,SIPT+n." pairs share a
! serial the same way).  So line 49's statement is the SECOND
! statement of line 48's card, and the listing indents it two
! characters, which is the same tell printed p.169 line 9 carries.
!
! >>> THE SURVEY IS WRONG AT BOTH ENDS AND LOSES THIRTY ROWS. <<<
! Run FRESH, not read out of the cache:
!
!     $ python3 strap/mcp_survey.py --pages 184 --reparse --report
!      PDF printed  off  rows    +       first       last  kind
!      184     177    7    26    0   2C0701.4C  220726.00  code
!
! against this page's 56 lines, 220700.00 .. 220741.00.  It loses the
! FIRST row and the LAST row and twenty-eight in between; its "first"
! is not even octal ("2C0701.4C", a C in a field that can only hold
! 0-7, which is the octal-field argument firing on the survey's own
! output); and it DISAGREES WITH THE CACHED RUN for the same page,
! which reported 220701.40 .. 220726.4.  Two runs of one tool on one
! page, two different last locations.  Nothing in this deck comes
! from either.
!
!   lines 1-3    the banner.  Counted MECHANICALLY off the 600-dpi
!                ink, by glyph runs across x=4770..9060, not by eye:
!                line 2 is a lone "-", FIFTEEN asterisks, two blanks,
!                "IDENTIFIER", two blanks, FIFTEEN asterisks, a lone
!                "-" (42 runs, and "IDENTIFIER" accounts for ten of
!                them).  Lines 1 and 3 are full-width asterisk rules
!                of SEVENTY characters each -- their runs merge at
!                this resolution (70 and 72 counted), so the figure
!                is derived from the span 4844..9032 against the
!                60-pixel character pitch line 2 measures.  Each of
!                the three carries a lone "-" in the NAME column and
!                starts its asterisk run at the STATEMENT column.
!
!   line 4       "SLC,$".  Its printed LOCATION, 220700.00, is the
!                counter ARRIVING from printed p.176.  It carries a
!                location-column asterisk.
!
!   lines 5-56   the routine, K FRONT onward.
!
! C22-6728-1 names it in typeset prose: "control is given to the
! identifier routine (KFRONT)" and "The identifier is entered at
! KFRONT (Figure 18)".  Both quotes were read first-hand out of
! docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt, at its PDF
! pp.31 and 32 -- and in that OCR the printed footers 30, 32 and 33
! fall on PDF pages 30, 32 and 33, so printed page = PDF page there.
! The same file's Table 2 lists KFRONT as an ENTRY symbol whose EXIT
! is SDISP.  This page is that entry and its first FIFTY-TWO
! statements; the routine runs off the bottom of the page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE BACKWARD JOIN IS CLOSED THREE WAYS, ALL FROM OUTSIDE THIS
!     PAGE, AND ALL THREE AGREE. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!  1. printed p.176's line 48 is "BD,SIPT+47." at 220677.40, a HALF
!     word, so its counter leaves at 220700.00.  This page's printed
!     "SLC,$" prints 220700.00 -- and an SLC emits nothing, so that
!     printed location IS the arriving counter, written by IBM's own
!     assembler.  The join is read, not assumed.
!  2. decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap carries "KFRONT SYN,(8)220700.0"
!     with the !CHECK "215501.40 | 220700.32 42 | line 19 BXL,K
!     FRONT".  0o32 has the 0o40 bit CLEAR, so that page pins K
!     FRONT's HALF WORD to 220700.00.  This page PRINTS the defining
!     card: line 5's NAME column is "K FRONT" against the printed
!     LOCATION 220700.00.
!  3. decks p.146, p.159 and p.169 all carry "KIODRN SYN,(8)220706.40"
!     and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p167.strap carries "KNI SYN,
!     (8)220726.40".  This page PRINTS both defining cards, at
!     220706.40 (line 16) and 220726.40 (line 42).  Four landed decks,
!     read off three different pages' branch instructions, against
!     this page's NAME column: all four agree to the half word.
!
! So every one of printed p.176's three falsifiable predictions for
! this page held, and the two it listed as already-agreeing witnesses
! are now the page's own printed cards.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS PAGE CANNOT SEE -- READ BEFORE TRUSTING A BIT OFFSET
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THERE IS NO "SIC" ANYWHERE ON THIS PAGE. <<<  Checked by eye
! over all fifty-six lines and by the assembled source below.  So the
! exception docs/transcription_workflow.md records -- a SIC reads its
! operand's full 24-bit bit address -- does NOT apply here, and every
! external this page SYNs off a BRANCH is known only to the HALF
! WORD.  Bit 32 IS checked (a wrong half word fails), bits 0-31 are
! not observable from this page.  That covers all ten of the forward
! references below.
!
! THE BIT-ADDRESSED OPERANDS ARE DIFFERENT and ARE pinned, because a
! BRANCH ON BIT prints the whole 24-bit bit address of the bit it
! tests:
!   line 21  "BB,S L,K MCP"  prints 215001.04, which pins S L to the
!            BIT at 215001.04 -- and printed p.103 line 14's defining
!            card is where the (BU,1) comes from, not from here.
!   lines 37, 46, 47, 50 print 000000.33 / .34 / .35 / .36, pinning
!            S MULTI, S UN AVL, S UN ASG and S UN SUP to bits 27, 28,
!            29 and 30 of the unit block -- every one agreeing with
!            printed p.99's defining cards digit for digit.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK: THREE OF THEM, AND NO RULE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Found MECHANICALLY, by counting ink in the 600-dpi band x=2630..2900
! (between the LOCATION column and the BINARY OUTPUT column) on each
! of the fifty-six rows.  Exactly three rows have ink there and the
! other fifty-three have none:
!
!     line  4   220700.00   the printed "SLC,$"
!     line 23   220713.00   "BXH,ZIOD H"      -BRANCH IF IOD OUT OF RANGE
!     line 42   220726.40   "K NI  KVI,3,11.32"
!
! WHAT THIS PAGE ELIMINATES, on its own ink:
!   * NOT "every row with a NAME":  lines 5, 16, 27 and 51 carry
!     NAMEs (K FRONT, K IOD RN, K SOAR, K K NI) and NO asterisk,
!     while line 42 carries both.
!   * NOT "every branch":  this page carries SEVENTEEN branch
!     instructions and two of them are marked.
!   * NOT "every full word" and NOT "every half word":  line 23 is a
!     half word at an even boundary, line 42 a half word at an odd
!     one, line 4 emits nothing at all.
!   * NOT "the first card of a card deck":  LA000001 is line 1 and is
!     unmarked.
!
! A HYPOTHESIS AND THE PAGE THAT ALREADY KILLS IT.  The three marked
! lines are 4, 23 and 42 -- EXACTLY NINETEEN APART, twice.  That is
! the only arithmetic this page offers and it is a coincidence:
! measured over the landed decks pp.160-176, the gaps between
! consecutive marked lines are 10, 13, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23,
! 31 and 38.  printed p.165 (gaps 21 then 10) and printed p.174 (gap
! 38) each refute "every nineteenth line" by themselves.  Recorded and
! dropped.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT strap_asm REFUSED -- THE PRINTED FORM WAS HANDED TO IT FIRST
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE CARDS WERE REFUSED AS PRINTED, all the same defect, the one
! the brief lists as a known gap: A BLANK INSIDE A NAME INSIDE AN
! EXPRESSION.  The bare name resolves; the name plus "+n." or "-.32"
! does not.  Measured, verbatim:
!
!     SVA,2,K IOD RN-.32      -> AssemblerError "undefined symbol 'K'"
!     SVA,2,K IOD RN          -> assembles
!
! The three are lines 11, 13 and 19 and each is labelled at its own
! card below.  NOTHING ELSE was substituted: every other card on this
! page is the page's own characters, blanks and all, including the
! four DIFFERENT spellings of one symbol on lines 20, 23, 25 and 28
! (see below).  The substitution closes blanks and changes nothing
! else, and the printed form is recorded beside each one.
!
! >>> THE PAGE IS ITS OWN PROOF THAT A BLANK IS NOT SIGNIFICANT. <<<
! Lines 20, 23, 25 and 28 branch to ONE symbol and print it FOUR
! different ways -- "Z  IODH", "ZIOD H", "ZIOD H", "Z  IOD H" -- and
! all four compile to the same address, 221002.00, in the same
! operand position.  That is the strongest rung of
! docs/transcription_workflow.md 2b (the same statement printed twice
! on one page) applied to BLANKS rather than to ink, and it is why
! writing the printed blanks is safe wherever the assembler takes
! them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE OF THE 56 PRINTED ROWS CHECKS, FIRST RUN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All thirty-four assembled words reproduce the BINARY OUTPUT column
! exactly, both half words of every full-word instruction included.
! Two rows deserve naming because the ink alone would not have settled
! them:
!
!   line 30 "V-I,2,1.32" prints its byte as what looks like "CD" at
!           600 dpi.  It is 0D.  The row's own octal field prints
!           "C0CC01.45" -- four impossible C's, the octal-field
!           argument of docs/transcription_workflow.md 2b rung 5 --
!           so this row demonstrably drops ink on round glyphs, and
!           the control is line 8's "V+I,2,.32" at 000000.45 05 two
!           rows up: V- sets 0x08 against V+'s 0x00 and nothing else
!           moves.  Assembler and page agree on 0D.
!   line 51 "SV,2,S ACT AD($13)" -- the last glyph of the symbol is a
!           D and not a C.  Settled three ways and not by shape: the
!           row's own comment is "-ACTUATED ADDR TO FILE AREA"
!           (ADDRESS), the byte .45 requires the operand at bit 32,
!           and printed p.103's defining card is "SACTAD SYN(BU,19),
!           0.32  -ACTUATED ADDRESS".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! JOINING THIS PAGE TO THE BODY IMAGE -- I COULD NOT MAKE THE EDIT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The brief forbids writing under tests/, so the registration is
! NOT done.  The edit is two lines in tests/check_mcp_body_image.py:
!
!     FIRST, LAST = 99, 176      ->   FIRST, LAST = 99, 177
!     check("body_page_count", len(pages), 77)   ->   78
!
! and NOT strap/mcp_image.py's MCP_IPL_PAGES, which is the IPL
! assembly and a different program.  MEASURED, by splicing this deck
! into check_mcp_body_image.body_pages() from a scratch script: the
! merge succeeds, and KFRONT, KIODRN and KNI stop being stand-ins and
! become PLACES -- their four landed stand-ins are dropped only
! because they agreed with this page's printed cards first.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! MEASURED INJECTION, run, with what it actually printed
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The claim that the merge CHECKS this page's origin rather than
! accepting it has to be falsifiable, so it was falsified on purpose.
! Move this deck's SLC one half word, to "SLC,(8)220700.40", change
! nothing else, and re-run the splice:
!
!     FAIL KFRONT: printed p.117 SYNs bit 4747264,
!                  printed p.177 places it at bit 4747296
!
! So the join is checked by the image and not merely asserted here.
! With the printed origin the same splice reports:
!
!     pages: 78
!     MERGE OK: 700 defined, 69 external
!     origin 0o215000  last 0o220741
!     unaccounted: 0
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 1. THE THIRD LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK.  Four eliminations above and
!    no rule.  Lines 23 and 42 have nothing in common that lines 20,
!    28 and 41 (same mnemonics, same shapes) lack.
! 2. ONE COMMENT GLYPH, line 6: "-TURN OFF S?OP BIT".  The second
!    letter is a vertical stem with a bottom bar and a short middle
!    stub -- an L with a spatter, or an E whose top bar dropped.  The
!    page's own reference glyphs (line 15's "LVE") print L with no
!    middle bar and E with a HEAVY top bar, which argues for L, but
!    the stub is real.  The manual oracle is SILENT: grep over all of
!    docs/ocr/ returns zero hits for both SLOP and SEOP, and
!    "TURN OFF S..." in those files yields only SC, SIR, SU variants.
!    Neither reading is an English word, so the comment column cannot
!    arbitrate itself.  Recorded here as printed; it compiles nothing
!    and no check can see it.  What would settle it: another page
!    printing the same comment, or any MCP document naming the field
!    that lives at bits 19-23 of an index register's value.
! 3. THE BIT OFFSET OF ALL TEN FORWARD EXTERNALS.  No SIC on this
!    page (see above), so they are half-word readings and the ".0"
!    each one carries is a CONVENTION, not a measurement.
! 4. WHY THE IDENTIFIER'S FIRST ACT IS "CM0000(BU,5),$3.19".  It
!    zeroes five bits at bit 19 of index register 3's value field,
!    which is the low five bits of that value's bit-offset -- i.e. it
!    rounds $3 down to a half-word boundary.  That reading is
!    arithmetic, not a citation, and is not in the deck.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
