        BB,S UN ASG($11),K ASIGN     ! line 47  as printed
        KVI,3,D CCW                  ! line 48  as printed
        BXE,K OP OK                  ! line 49  as printed; SAME CARD SERIAL as line 48 (LA000048) and indented two characters -- the semicolon one-card form  -IF $CCW, SKIP + PROCEED
        BBZ,S UN SUP($11),K 2 INT    ! line 50  as printed  -CHECK IF INT IS STACKED
KKNI    SV,2,S ACT AD($13)           ! line 51  NAME printed "K K NI"  -ACTUATED ADDR TO FILE AREA
        SV,13,S FI AAC($12)          ! line 52  as printed  -ACTUATED FILE A ADD TO UNIT A
        L(BU,1),.55($2)              ! line 53  as printed
        ST(BU,1),SSEOP($11)          ! line 54  as printed
        LFI(BU,6),(2)100000,1        ! line 55  as printed
        ST(BU,7),SCCW+.18($13)       ! line 56  as printed; a FULL word, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220742.00

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKS.  Fifty-two emitting rows, fifty-two !CHECK lines, every
! one the BINARY OUTPUT column exactly as printed.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM KFRONT  220700.00
!SYM KIODRN  220706.40
!SYM KSOAR   220715.40
!SYM KNI     220726.40
!SYM KKNI    220735.00
!
!CHECK 220700.00 | 000040.07 04 | line 5 K FRONT KVI,3,32.0 -- the immediate is a bit address: 32 words is 0o40, and .07 is the KVI operation bits (line 12's "2.0" prints 000002.07 and line 42's "11.32" prints 000013.47, which is 0o13 words OR 0o40 bits OR 0o07)
!CHECK 220700.40 | 000023.23 80 005000.00 F0 | line 6 CM0000(BU,5),$3.19 -- $3 is index register 3 at word 0o23 and bit 19 DECIMAL is 0o23, which is why both fields print 23; the four connective bits are all round glyphs in a field that can only hold 0 or 1, so they are 0000
!CHECK 220701.40 | 220761.72 40 | line 7 BZXL,K PLUG1 -- 0o32 is the XL indicator's address bits and 0o72 is 0o32 OR 0o40, so K PLUG1's HALF WORD is 220761.40. Byte 40 distinguishes BZXL from BXL (42)
!CHECK 220702.00 | 000000.45 05 | line 8 V+I,2,.32 -- an immediate index operand: .32 DECIMAL is 0o40, index 2 contributes 0o04 and the operation bit 0o01
!CHECK 220702.40 | 220706.45 D0 | line 9 SVA,2,K IOD RN -- K IOD RN is THIS PAGE's line 16 at 220706.40, so 0o40 OR index 2's 0o04 OR 0o01 is 0o45. An internal reference, so this is a real check of placement and not of a SYN
!CHECK 220703.00 | 000000.45 05 | line 10 V+I,2,.32 -- the IDENTICAL card to line 8, which is its control
!CHECK 220703.40 | 220706.05 D0 | line 11 SVA,2,K IOD RN-.32 -- 220706.40 less 32 bits is 220706.00, so the 0o40 drops and only index 2's 0o04 and the 0o01 remain. The printed octal field reads "220706.C5"; a C cannot occur in an octal field, so it is 0o05
!CHECK 220704.00 | 000002.07 04 | line 12 KVI,3,2.0 -- the control for line 48, which compiles the SAME WORD from the symbol D CCW
!CHECK 220704.40 | 000022.00 80 215247.04 E0 | line 13 SWAPI,2,$2,S TLR+15. -- $2 is index register 2 at word 0o22; S TLR+15 is FIFTEEN WORDS past 215230, printing 215247, which is what makes "+15." a word count. The mirror of line 19
!CHECK 220705.40 | 220706.73 42 | line 14 BXH,K IOD RN -- 0o33 is the XH indicator's bits, OR 0o40 for K IOD RN's half word. Byte 42 is the plain (non-BZ) form
!CHECK 220706.00 | 220706.01 B0 | line 15 LVE,0,$ -- $ is 220706.00 itself; .01 is 2J+1 = 1 for J=0, the same shape printed p.169 line 6 carries
!CHECK 220706.40 | 220706.43 B0 | line 16 K IOD RN LVE,1,$ -- $ is 220706.40, so 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 3 for J=1. This row DEFINES the symbol four landed decks SYN at (8)220706.40
!CHECK 220707.00 | 220707.50 C6 | line 17 BUSAZ,$+.32 -- $ is 220707.00 so the target is 220707.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o10. C6 is BUSAZ against BUSA's C2 and the Z IS visible here, this being a branch and not a reservation
!CHECK 220707.40 | 220710.10 46 | line 18 BADZ,$+.32 -- target 220710.00, printing the bare 0o10. 46 is BADZ against BAD's 42
!CHECK 220710.00 | 215247.00 80 000022.04 E0 | line 19 SWAPI,2,S TLR+15.,$2 -- the two addresses of line 13 exchanged, which is what makes the pair each other's control: A1 is a 24-bit bit address and A2 a 19-bit half-word address, and both forms print the same two numbers
!CHECK 220711.00 | 221002.31 42 | line 20 BXVZ,Z  IODH -- 0o31 is the XVZ indicator's bits and there is no 0o40, so Z IOD H's half word is 221002.00
!CHECK 220711.40 | 215001.04 80 221000.34 02 | line 21 BB,S L,K MCP -- a BRANCH ON BIT prints the tested bit's FULL 24-bit address, so this row pins S L to the BIT at 215001.04, agreeing with printed p.103's defining card. 0o34 in the second word is the 111 of the identifying literal at bits 51-53 with the half-word bit CLEAR, so K MCP is 221000.00
!CHECK 220712.40 | 215005.42 90 | line 22 KV,1,S MAX RN -- index 1 contributes 0o02, so 0o42 is 0o40 OR 0o02 and S MAX RN's half word is 215005.40, which is printed p.103 line 36's "SMAXRN VF,0" plus a half word
!CHECK 220713.00 | 221002.33 42 | line 23 BXH,ZIOD H -- the SAME target as line 20 spelled differently and tested on a different indicator: 0o33 is XH where 0o31 is XVZ, and the address half is identical. This LOCATION carries the page's second asterisk
!CHECK 220713.40 | 000021.22 80 007000.20 50 | line 24 L(BU,7),$1.18 -- $1 is index register 1 at word 0o21 and bit 18 DECIMAL is 0o22
!CHECK 220714.40 | 221002.34 C0 | line 25 BZRZ,ZIOD H -- 0o34 is the RZ indicator's bits; byte C0 is the branch-if-zero form. Third spelling of the same symbol, same address
!CHECK 220715.00 | 215005.02 B0 | line 26 V+,1,S BA PP -- index 1's 0o02 with no 0o40, so S BA PP is 215005.00, a half word below S MAX RN
!CHECK 220715.40 | 000000.30 31 | line 27 K SOAR LV,12,0.0($1) -- index 12 is 0b1100 in bits 19-22, printing 0o30; the byte's low nibble 1 is the index $1
!CHECK 220716.00 | 221002.31 42 | line 28 BXVZ,Z  IOD H -- BIT-IDENTICAL to line 20 and spelled a FOURTH way. One page, one drum, one symbol, four blankings, one address: this is what proves a blank is not significant here
!CHECK 220716.40 | 000000.72 31 | line 29 LV,13,.32($1) -- index 13 is 0b1101, printing 0o32, OR the operand's 0o40
!CHECK 220717.00 | 000001.45 0D | line 30 V-I,2,1.32 -- word 1 plus a half word, plus index 2's 0o04 and the 0o01. The byte prints as "CD" and is 0D: the row's own octal field prints "C0CC01", four impossible C's, and line 8's V+I prints 05 where V- sets 0x08
!CHECK 220717.40 | 000000.24 3C | line 31 LV,10,0.0($12) -- index 10 is 0b1010, printing 0o24; low nibble C is $12
!CHECK 220720.00 | 000032.34 30 | line 32 LV,14,$10 -- $10 is index register 10 at word 0o32; index 14 is 0b1110, printing 0o34; no offset index, so the low nibble is 0
!CHECK 220720.40 | 000032.24 B0 | line 33 V+,10,$10 -- the same register as line 32 read by index 10, printing 0o24
!CHECK 220721.00 | 215002.24 B0 | line 34 V+,10,S CHAN S -- S CHAN S is 215002.00, printed p.103's "SYN,SXCHAN"; half word only
!CHECK 220721.40 | 000000.64 8A 004066.60 50 | line 35 L(BU,4),S EQUIP($10),-19 -- 000000.64 is bit 52 of the unit block, which IS printed p.99 line 38's "SEQUIP SYN(BU,4),0.52" read back off an instruction; low nibble A is the index $10 and the -19 offset is in the second word
!CHECK 220722.40 | 000010.10 30 | line 36 LV,4,$L -- $L is the accumulator's left half at word 8 = 0o10, and index 4 is 0b0100, also printing 0o10. The two 0o10s are different fields that happen to coincide
!CHECK 220723.00 | 000000.33 8A 221003.74 00 | line 37 BZB,S MULTI($10),K UNA -- the bit branch prints S MULTI's full bit address, 27 DECIMAL = 0o33, agreeing with printed p.99 line 24. 0o74 is 0o34 OR 0o40, so K UNA is 221003.40; byte 00 is BZB against BB's 02
!CHECK 220724.00 | 000000.26 3A | line 38 LV,11,0.0($10) -- index 11 is 0b1011, printing 0o26; low nibble A is $10
!CHECK 220724.40 | 000000.66 BC | line 39 V+,11,0.32($12) -- 0o26 OR the operand's 0o40; low nibble C is $12
!CHECK 220725.00 | 000000.63 8B 002000.20 50 | line 40 L(BU,2),S MOUNT($11) -- 0o63 is bit 51, printed p.70's "SMOUNT SYN(BU,1),0.51"; this row reads it with a (BU,2) of its own, so the LENGTH here is the statement's and not the symbol's
!CHECK 220726.00 | 221004.74 C0 | line 41 BZRZ,K NO GO -- 0o74 is 0o34 OR 0o40, so K NO GO is 221004.40
!CHECK 220726.40 | 000013.47 04 | line 42 K NI KVI,3,11.32 -- 11 words and 32 bits is 0o13 and 0o40, OR the KVI bits 0o07. This row DEFINES the symbol printed p.167 SYNs at (8)220726.40, and its LOCATION carries the page's third asterisk
!CHECK 220727.00 | 220771.32 40 | line 43 BZXL,K C OP -- 0o32 with no 0o40, so K C OP is 220771.00. Same mnemonic and same byte as line 7, which is its control
!CHECK 220727.40 | 000000.31 8A 002077.20 50 | line 44 L(BU,2),S CH AVL($10),-2 -- 0o31 is bit 25, printed p.99 line 21's "SCHAVL SYN(BU,1),0.25"; the -2 offset is in the second word
!CHECK 220730.40 | 221004.74 C0 | line 45 BZRZ,K NO GO -- BIT-IDENTICAL to line 41, which is its control
!CHECK 220731.00 | 000000.34 8B 221154.34 02 | line 46 BB,S UN AVL($11),Z E1 -- 0o34 is bit 28, printed p.99 line 26. The second word's 0o34 has the half-word bit clear, so Z E1 is 221154.00; byte 02 is BB
!CHECK 220732.00 | 000000.35 8B 221077.74 02 | line 47 BB,S UN ASG($11),K ASIGN -- 0o35 is bit 29, printed p.99 line 27; 0o74 puts K ASIGN at 221077.40
!CHECK 220733.00 | 000002.07 04 | line 48 KVI,3,D CCW -- BIT-IDENTICAL to line 12's "KVI,3,2.0". Two statements, one page, one word: this pins D CCW to 2.0 on this page's own ink and confirms printed p.102's defining card
!CHECK 220733.40 | 220743.32 C2 | line 49 BXE,K OP OK -- 0o32 is the XE indicator's bits (XE is 53, XL is 52, and both print 0o32; the byte C2 against line 43's 40 is what separates them), so K OP OK is 220743.00. SAME CARD as line 48
!CHECK 220734.00 | 000000.36 8B 221067.74 06 | line 50 BBZ,S UN SUP($11),K 2 INT -- 0o36 is bit 30, printed p.99 line 28; 0o74 puts K 2 INT at 221067.40; byte 06 is BBZ against BB's 02 and BZB's 00
!CHECK 220735.00 | 000000.45 3D | line 51 K K NI SV,2,S ACT AD($13) -- 0o45 is 0o40 (S ACT AD at bit 32) OR index 2's 0o04 OR 0o01; low nibble D is $13, read on its straight left stem. The symbol's last letter is D and not C: the comment says ADDR and printed p.103 line 5 says ADDRESS
!CHECK 220735.40 | 000003.33 3C | line 52 SV,13,S FI AAC($12) -- word 3, printed p.101 line 13's "SFIAAC SYN(BU,18),3.0"; index 13 is 0b1101, printing 0o32, OR the 0o01
!CHECK 220736.00 | 000000.67 82 001000.20 50 | line 53 L(BU,1),.55($2) -- bit 55 DECIMAL is 0o67, written bare and so a literal bit offset in word 0; low nibble 2 is the index $2
!CHECK 220737.00 | 000000.56 8B 001000.20 D0 | line 54 ST(BU,1),SSEOP($11) -- 0o56 is bit 46, printed p.99 line 34's "SSEOP SYN(BU,1),0.46". The second word differs from line 53's only in the store bit
!CHECK 220740.00 | 400000.00 80 406000.46 70 | line 55 LFI(BU,6),(2)100000,1 -- the immediate is LEFT-JUSTIFIED in the 24-bit field, so 0b100000 lands in the top six bits and prints 400000.00; the ",1" offset is in the second word
!CHECK 220741.00 | 000004.22 8D 007000.20 D0 | line 56 ST(BU,7),SCCW+.18($13) -- word 4 (printed p.102 line 15's "SCCW SYN(BU,64),4.0") plus 18 DECIMAL bits = 0o22; low nibble D is $13. A FULL WORD, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220742.00, which is what printed p.178 must print

